Third-party components

OpenSVN bundles an Apache Subversion runtime on macOS (strategy: ADR-0003).
The bundled binaries and libraries remain under their own licenses; the full
text of each license must be shipped inside the application bundle under
`Contents/Resources/licenses/` before any public release.

Current inventory (recorded 2026-10-18, macOS arm64, Homebrew svn 1.14.5):

  subversion, serf, apr, apr-util, openssl@3   Apache-2.0
  lz4                                          BSD-2-Clause
  utf8proc                                     MIT AND Unicode-DFS-2015
  gettext (libintl)                            GPL-3.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later

NOTE: `libintl` is the one compliance-sensitive dependency. The preferred fix is
to build the bundled runtime with `--disable-nls`, removing the dependency
entirely (SVN's own message catalogues are not used by OpenSVN's UI).

